# Enfusion vehicle paint and materials

Split from `enfusion-enforce.mdc`, whose rules for adding a fact apply here: one bullet, **Claim.** Consequence. Evidence. Add a Changelog line in `enfusion-enforce.mdc`.

## Meshes and materials at run time

- **Changing a live vehicle hull's mesh from script crashes the engine a frame later.** `SetObject` (a `$remap` included) and `SetVObjectFromPrefab` build a new mesh instance and free the old one, while `VehicleAnimationComponent` still holds a mesh binder on the old one. The call returns and the paint shows, then PostFrame dies in `VehicleUpdateSignalsSystem` / `VehicleUpdateAnimsSystem` (`Access violation. Illegal read … at 0x30`). `RebindEntity`, deactivating and reactivating the entity, and keeping a `ref` to the old `VObject` did not prevent it. UH-1H seat parts took the call without crashing; hull, rotors and cockpit panel did not — do not build on a subset. Never change a vehicle mesh at runtime. Recolour its materials (next bullet); a prefab variant sets which materials it names with `MeshObject` `Materials` entries (a child's entries merge with its parent's; slotted parts need their own variant via the hull's `SlotManagerComponent`). Evidence: `runtime: logs_2026-09-30_21-32-54` (crash 41 ms after the paint, stack resolved from exe strings); `IA_HeliSkinLiveProbe` mode 3 crash `logs_2026-10-01_00-57-10`; vanilla `UH1H_sharkNose.et`.
- **`Material.GetOrLoadMaterial(emat, 0).SetParam(name, value)` recolours live meshes at once, with no entity operation.** A UH-1H with a pilot seated and the engine running took 20 changes 150 ms apart without a crash, and its hull `VObject` stayed the same. A `Material` is shared by every entity naming that `.emat`, so setting a vanilla material recolours every user; a prefab variant naming its own `.emat` copies (each inheriting the vanilla one) changes alone. A material set before any entity used it showed on the entity spawned later, while a script `ref` held it. `ResetParam` goes to the material *class* default (white for a colour), not the `.emat`'s value. `Material` has no getters, and the change is local to the machine: replicate the intent and set it on every machine that renders. Evidence: `Core/generated/Visual/Material.c`; `IA_HeliSkinLiveProbe` modes 301 and 2, `logs_2026-10-01_00-52-47` and `00-53-46` (screenshots: only the set channel's Huey changed). Not yet seen in multiplayer or after streaming out.
- **`SetParam` on the colour layers of a `MatPBRMulti` hull paints a camouflage-textured helicopter one flat colour.** The Mi-8MT's camouflage is the layers `Color_1`, `Color_2` and `Color_3` of `Mi8_Body.emat`; setting all three to one colour gave a plain hull in play mode, engine running, with the slotted parts on twinned materials following. Which layer is which differs per helicopter: paint each layer a loud colour on its own airframe to find out. Evidence: `IA_HeliSkinLiveProbe` mode 5 `logs_2026-10-01_13-14-14`; livery sheets `13-32-07`, `13-35-53`; engine running `13-37-01`.
- **A tinted `Specular` / `SpecularIBL` on a hull material shows through dark paint.** The Mi-8's are khaki, and a black or grey livery came out with a khaki sheen until the channel material set them neutral (`0.39` / `0.74` grey) while a livery is on. Evidence: Mi-8 livery sheets, `logs_2026-10-01_13-32-07` to `13-38-01`.
- **`delete entity` on an Mi-8 in a script-created `Preview` world leaks `GameEnvironmentProbeEntity` script instances at exit.** `Leaked 'GameEnvironmentProbeEntity' script instance (96x)` after an asset check that spawned and deleted every Mi-8 twin; the plugin's exit code was still its own. Evidence: `IA_HeliSkinAssetCheck`, `logs_2026-10-01_13-30-26`.
- **`UVSrcDetail "UV world"` on a vehicle hull is a top-down projection in the model's own space, not in the world.** A `MatPBRMulti` hull given it in a channel `.emat` kept a 2.5 m blob on the same spot through a 3 m move, a 40° and 90° yaw and a 90° roll, on every panel regardless of the mesh UVs; the roof shows the shape, vertical walls smear it into vertical streaks. It moves every detail layer, not only the paint. The same texture on `"UV set 2"` breaks at each UV island. The shaders offer only `UV set 1`, `UV set 2`, `UV world`. `SetParam("BCR_1", textureName)` returns false, so the pattern must be in the `.emat`. Evidence: `IA_HeliCamoProbe` mode 3 and 5, `logs_2026-10-01_12-25-33`, `12-27-18`, `12-21-11`.
- **`World.CreateDecal` on a live helicopter renders and follows it, but paints only some surfaces.** On the UH-1H blobs stuck to glass, marking quads and one rear panel, never to doors, nose or mid tail boom, whatever the size, depth, direction, material class or depth bias. A non-null `Decal` does not mean visible paint (rotor and seat parts metres away returned one). A `Material.Create(name, "MatPBRDecal", params)` name works as `materialName` and takes the decal colour; about 180 decals cost 2 ms. Evidence: `IA_HeliCamoProbe` mode 9, `logs_2026-10-01_12-17-55`.

## Reading materials and prefabs

- **An `.emat`'s values can be read with `Resource.Load(emat).GetResource().ToBaseContainer()`.** A colour comes back only as a string `"r g b a"` (`Get` into `float[4]` or `vector` fails); a number as `float`. A parameter the file does not set reads empty: walk `GetAncestor()`. One that no file in the chain sets (vanilla `UH_1H_Interior01` `Color_4`) has only the class default, so `ResetParam` is right for it. Evidence: `IA_HeliSkinAssetCheck` FAIL `logs_2026-10-01_00-49-02`, PASS `00-49-52`. Workbench only; unproven in a packed build.
- **`BaseContainer` lists what an `.emat` sets.** `GetNumVars` / `GetVarName` / `GetDataVarType` enumerate the class's parameters, and `IsVariableSetDirectly(name)` plus a walk over `GetAncestor()` says which ones a file in the chain sets. `BaseContainerTools.SaveContainer(source, ResourceName.Empty, "$profile:x.conf")` dumps a container as text. Evidence: `IA_HeliPaintSurvey`, `logs_2026-10-01_12-51-14` to `12-59-40`.
- **`Resource.Load("{GUID}")` with the GUID alone resolves**, and `GetResource().ToBaseContainer().GetResourceName()` gives the full `{GUID}path`. Evidence: `IA_HeliPaintSurvey`, `logs_2026-10-01_12-51-14` to `12-59-40`.
- **`VObject.GetMaterials` repeats each slot once per LOD.** Dedupe by slot name. Same log.
- **A prefab's component GUIDs and root `ID` are not exposed by the container API, but its text is readable.** `BaseContainer.GetName()` is empty for components and `MaterialAssignClass` entries. `FileIO.OpenFile(prefab.GetPath(), FileMode.READ)` reads the `.et` text, from a pak too, and the ids can be parsed from it (`string.IndexOfFrom`, `StartsWith` and `Replace` exist). `source.GetObjectArray("components")` on a child prefab is the merged view with its ancestors. Evidence: `IA_HeliPaintSurvey`, `logs_2026-10-01_12-51-14` to `12-59-40`. Seen on vanilla paks in Workbench only; a modded pak is not yet tried.
